# Discovery — {{ project_name }}

Read-only intake step. Fetches a ticket from {{ tracker_label }}, parses its Acceptance
Criteria into a structured list, and surfaces any prior Test Design docs or test cases.
Outputs a typed `discovery_payload` for downstream skills and agents.

## When to Invoke

- At the start of every QA session for a new ticket
- Before test-design-agent runs (the main agent may run this first to confirm preconditions)
- When a human asks "what's the current state of ticket PROJ-1234?"

## Steps

### 1. Fetch the ticket

{% if tracker == 'jira' %}
```
getJiraIssue({ key: "{{ tracker_project_key }}-NNNN" })
```
Read: title, description, Acceptance Criteria field, labels, assignee, linked issues.
{% elif tracker == 'github_issues' %}
```
GET /repos/{{ tracker_project_key }}/issues/NNN
```
Read: title, body, labels, linked PRs. Parse AC bullets from the issue body.
{% elif tracker == 'linear' %}
Use the Linear API to fetch the issue by identifier.
Read: title, description, sub-issues. Parse AC bullets from the description.
{% elif tracker == 'azure_devops' %}
Use the Azure DevOps API to fetch the work item from project `{{ tracker_project_key }}`.
Read: title, description, acceptance criteria field, linked work items.
{% else %}
Fetch the ticket from {{ tracker_label }} using its native API.
Read the title, description, and acceptance criteria.
{% endif %}

### 2. Parse Acceptance Criteria

Extract every AC bullet as a structured list:
```json
[
  { "id": "AC-1", "text": "...", "type": "functional | constraint | non-functional" }
]
```
If no ACs are found: set `has_acs = false` and surface as a blocker.

### 3. Search for prior work

{% if doc_platform == 'confluence' %}
Search Confluence for pages whose title contains the ticket key.
{% elif doc_platform == 'notion' %}
Search the QA Test Designs database for pages tagged with the ticket key.
{% elif doc_platform == 'github_wiki' %}
Search the `{{ tracker_project_key }}` Wiki for pages containing the ticket key.
{% else %}
Search `.qa/designs/` for files named `<ticket-key>*.md`.
{% endif %}

{% if has_test_repo %}
Search {{ test_repo_label }} for cases where Refs contains the ticket key.
{% endif %}

Read `.claude/references/automation-coverage.md` for any existing automation rows for this ticket.

### 4. Output the discovery payload

```json
{
  "ticket_key":     "string",
  "title":          "string",
  "has_acs":        true,
  "acs":            [{ "id": "AC-1", "text": "...", "type": "..." }],
  "td_doc_id":      "string | null",
  "td_status":      "In Review | Approved | null",
  "test_case_ids":  ["list | empty"],
  "test_run_id":    "string | null",
  "automation_rows": ["list of case IDs already in automation-coverage.md"],
  "derived_phase":  "no_td | bdd | manual | automation | done | done_simple"
}
```

## Hard Rules

- Read-only — discovery never writes to any system.
- If `has_acs = false`, surface it immediately and do not advance the pipeline.
- The `derived_phase` field is advisory — the main agent makes the final routing decision.
